invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: a TCP host object packages the S-box table beside the AES
  instructions, where no public key exists for it to run and the only AES
  keys are traffic keys. A host object holds two ciphers only over QUIC,
  where the table runs the Initial and Retry keys (docs/decisions.md 81
  and 89). The lint's TCP suite host row bans quic_aes_soft.c.

--- old
             $(if $(filter quic-nonblocking,$(TRANSPORT)),quic_aes_soft.c),$(AES_IMPL)))
--- new
             quic_aes_soft.c,$(AES_IMPL)))
